# Project Overview > Project Details > Implementation

- 1. Sign-in Request User want to sign in the dApp by send a simple request with identity chain type, eg: DOT, KSM, ETH etc. The payload is required since each chain has its own algorithmic mechanism. request payload(1) { "identity-type": "dot" }
- 2. Authentication Requirement dApp will return the callback info. The callback endpoint is used by Identity provider to send signature data to dApp. { "identity-type": "dot", "callback-endpoint": "http://dapp.com/login/callback", "scope": ["xxx", "yyy"], "chanllenge": xxxxxxxxxx", }
- 3. Connect to Signer User sends request to the Identity Provider (Injected Signer like: Polkadot.js Extension, Metamask, Parity Signer …). This action will call up a browser extension or some other external applications.

"identity-type": "dot", "callback-endpoint": "http://dapp.com/login/callback", "scope": ["xxx", "yyy"], "chanllenge": xxxxxxxxxx", }

{ "identity-type": "dot", "public-key": "xxxxxxxx", "account-signed": "xxxxxxxxxx", "scope": ["xxx", "yyy"],

